 # Combat model
 
+## Dual Wield prototype v1 derivative (2026-10-29)
+
+The isolated prototype uses the upstream KH1 contact bridge and KH2 Valor data
+loaded from the player's own install. Only base ground PTYA rows with no ability
+requirement, air flag or hop are admitted. Each weapon retains its own animation
+and contact windows. Native air/casting/locomotion are outside the imported
+controller's ownership. These are deliberate prototype rules (high confidence
+as code policy; live timing/alignment still requires a fresh-process game test).
+
+The passive gate is one menu entry, id126, zero AP, initially unequipped. It
+does not grant any other ability or change AP/stats. Existing native Combo Plus
+and Combo Master copies are read without modification. Ability and native table
+preservation have synthetic unit coverage. No Drive request, resource drain,
+gauge, form tint, partner removal or form weapon slot is used. The duplicate
+loads the current KH1 weapon's own resource; a weapon/model binding change
+retires the old private pose and controller before re-admission. These are
+derivative design choices, not claims about KH2's original rules.
+
 This is what `combat-core` implements and where each piece comes from. Every rule is tagged:
 
 - **Data**: read straight from the game's tables (layouts documented by OpenKH).
-- 
