+## Dual Wield prototype v2 derivative (2026-10-29)
+
+**Observed in the supplied v1 recording:** long trail ribbons during combat. The user also
+reports that Sora's model sometimes appears away from his actual position. No matching native
+DLL log was supplied, so this is not an attribution of every visual glitch to one cause.
+
+**Confirmed code defects (high confidence):** v1's native-control exit did not always clear
+the primary trail flag, left trails were stepped only during the custom attack, duplicate
+poses kept placement and bones separately, and a private trail-owner model copy could pass
+the bone-count/distance admission heuristic. Custom placement could also be derived from the
+same output matrices the hook had overwritten. These are derivative lifecycle defects.
+
+**v2 policy (high confidence as implementation; live behavior unverified):** every custom
+exit retires the emitters; each blade uses its own Valor trail windows, or that blade's
+contact windows when its trail data cannot be read. A left emitter starts only after that
+attack tick's world pose is published for the exact current actor, instance, matrix array,
+weapon and room generation. A missing pose or discontinuity retires it. No enemy is required
+for a swing trail. Only successful native contacts produce impact feedback.
+
+Custom body poses use the skeleton pass's axes with the live actor's translation; they are
+never placed from the rewritten root. Native and imported duplicate poses publish complete
+world-space matrices together. Model copies belonging to menus or private effects are rejected
+by exact actor-instance identity. Invalid or excessive pose coordinates are not written.
+
+The user now requested Valor aerial combos and a KH2 idle. v2 admits ability-free Valor
+ground and aerial PTYA rows (ground hop rows remain excluded), and draws Valor's battle idle
+only over native standing-idle slots. Native locomotion, jumping outside attacks, casting,
+reactions, menus and scripted moves retain their ownership. A native jump/fall's recent
+measured velocity seeds aerial entry. On exit, native fall/casting resumes at the current
+height. This handoff is a derivative adaptation, not an exact KH2 physics claim.
+
+The single Dual Wield gate, default dual-blade contacts, current-weapon duplication, zero AP,
+no gauge/drain/transformation and no other ability grants remain the v1 policy. Synthetic
+coverage exercises the actual controller's aerial contact windows and the host's spatial/
+freshness policies. The optional real-game data paths and actual runtime handoffs still need
+a fresh-process KH1FM test with the native DLL log.
+
