@@ -1,5 +1,51 @@
 # Combat model
 
+## Dual Wield prototype v3 derivative (2026-10-29)
+
+**Evidence:** the supplied s341 native log loads six ability-free ground rows, six aerial
+rows and Valor idle, and reports successful native contacts. Its initial left-grip distance
+is 5.8 units versus the native right hold's roughly 4; the user's close-up shows the duplicate
+behind the palm. Those distances alone do not identify the correct palm direction.
+
+**Grip correction (high as coordinate policy; gameplay confirmation pending):** a hand-local
+weapon attachment must map the two bind frames' axes without carrying their global bind
+translations. v2 included the arm-length/spacing difference in the offset, then reused a
+right-hand calibration on the left. v3 strips both bind translations before computing that
+basis. The weapon-to-hand animation and native right-grip calibration remain. Synthetic
+checks cover translation invariance and a rotated current-hand attachment. No guessed
+world-space palm nudge or game skeleton data is embedded in source.
+
+**Run (derivative visual policy):** native ground run slots 5..7 receive Valor's run animation.
+Native movement, speed, collision, input and footstep logic remain KH1's. The donor loop is
+sampled from the current native motion clock divided by that motion's frame count. Native
+walk, jumping, reactions and scripts stay outside this visual gate. Neither run nor idle
+adds contacts or swing trails.
+
+**Master casting (derivative visual policy):** KH1 command type 2, spell ids 0..6, still calls
+the original command step. A new native motion request or clock restart is observed before
+creating a visual-only cast record. Sampling waits for the request to be consumed and for a
+cast header rather than the old idle/run/jump header. It requires the same actor/resource/
+room generation, native motion id and pointer, a valid native clock and bounded lifetime.
+Native motion changes, clock restarts without a new observation, damage, landing, unequip
+and transitions retire the overlay. Failed/busy commands do not start a donor by mere intent.
+
+The matching MAGC motion ids at the native spell's level select Master's own clips for Fire,
+Blizzard, Thunder and Cure (standard fallback ids 56/58, 59/61, 62/64, 65/67, ground/air).
+As in the upstream adaptation, Gravity uses Thunder, while Stop/Aero use Cure. Only body and
+two weapon poses are sampled. No Master controller, script, spell package, contacts, damage,
+resource rules or particle events run. Master weapon poses may float during their cast;
+their source is explicit and never changes the passive gate's active form state.
+
+The native live clock maps to normalized donor clip time, clamped at cast completion rather
+than looping. The donor's cumulative root curve is subtracted so its animation cannot pull
+the body away from the native actor or add Master's large cast lunges. Native KH1 alone owns
+spell effects, event timing, MP, damage, movement and cancels. This preserves native gameplay;
