 # Combat model
 
+## Dual Wield prototype v4 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**Request and source:** the user rejected v3's Master casts and requested matching Valor
+animations, including jump/fall. The pinned upstream `win/form.rs::Kind::magic_sub` returns
+`None` for Valor; its comments and `docs/drive-model.md` document magic being disabled there.
+That is the full form mod's behavior, not the passive ability's rule. This derivative keeps
+all KH1 spells usable and native. v3's command observer, cast policy and Master donor loading
+are removed. No replacement casting poses or donor spell scripts are installed.
+
+**Matching policy (high as code policy; live appearance unverified):** the known KH1 slot
+mapping in `win/pose.rs::play_for` supplies idle (0/1), walk (2..4), run (5..7), jump/rise
+(8/9 or 12/13), fall (10) and landing (11). Ground/air state checks exclude stale locomotion
+slots. Native movement states documented by `win/takeover.rs` add edge hang (13), edge climb
+(14) and glide (21), only when a current recognized motion header and donor clip exist.
+States for ladders, bars, swimming, flight, scripted movement and reactions are not inferred
+from nearby motion numbers. A donor missing from Valor's resolved motion/clip tables leaves
+that action native; readiness logs list all nine candidate matches and their availability.
+Base ground/aerial combo selection remains the v2 filtered Valor controller.
+
+**Clock policy:** visual sampling uses the current native motion clock and duration, never
+wall time or a donor controller. Each takeoff/rise pair is one normalized jump timeline:
+the first clip contributes its duration, then the rise continues after it. Each clip's FPS
+is accounted for, and changed/incomplete pair metadata rejects the overlay. Idle/walk/run,
+fall/hang/glide loop; landing and climbing clamp at the end. Pauses do not advance the pose.
+No animation pointer, native state, velocity or gameplay event is rewritten by this sampler.
+
+**Placement:** every non-attack visual subtracts its cumulative donor root curve before
+retargeting, so imported jump/climb travel cannot add to KH1 movement or displace the drawn
+body. An edge hang/climb adjusts the retargeted hand midpoint to KH1's native midpoint,
+bounded to 120 units. The target is taken before our pose write and retained only for the
+same actor generation and game frame. Repeated model passes cannot feed the just-written
+hands into a new target. A bad/missing target or phase returns to the current native pose.
+The root alone can remain constant between native and custom passes; the original hand
+snapshot is validated against the current pass before ledge alignment.
+
+Native KH1 still owns speed, jump height, gravity, collision, grabs, glide availability,
+spell animations/effects/MP/damage, items, reactions, specials, cancels and native events.
+No High Jump, Glide, guard, roll or recovery ability is granted by drawing a matching clip.
+Non-attack overlays execute no donor contacts, trails, effects or sounds. The zero-AP single
+ability, same-weapon duplication, grip calibration, contact isolation option, no gauge/drain/
+transformation and restoration on unequip remain unchanged.
+
+Synthetic tests cover matching/exclusion policy, both jump pairs across their boundary,
+different native clip rates, paused/one-shot clocks, rejected bad metadata, donor root
+removal and atomic bounded hand alignment. No real KH2 data path or native game execution
+was available here. Actual donor availability, animation blends, hand alignment, ground/air
+and ledge/glide transitions still require a fresh-process KH1FM video/log test.
+
