 # Combat model
 
+## Dual Wield prototype v5 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**Scope (user policy):** keep the duplicate visible on default KH1 animations, preserve
+equipped KH1 attack abilities, add matching Valor damage/item/interaction visuals and a
+cutscene idle. Default KH1 casting and the one zero-AP passive gate remain unchanged.
+
+**Native attack abilities (high as routing policy):** KH1's original command step already
+selects a row before `combat::exec` is called. The supplied Steam executable's command step
+uses a native hit/step counter, motion history and contextual ability checks before choosing
+finishers. v4 replaced those swings without maintaining all of that native state. Merely
+passing a finisher row through would not preserve its prerequisites. v5 keeps the whole
+affected combo lane under KH1 when a native action ability is equipped:
+
+| Lane | Equipped KH1 abilities that retain native routing |
+|---|---|
+| Ground | Vortex 17, Counterattack 19, Blitz 20, Slapshot 53, Sliding Dash 54, Ripple Drive 56, Stun Impact 57, Gravity Break 58, Zantetsuken 59 |
+| Air | Aerial Sweep 18, Hurricane Blast 55 |
+
+IDs come from the upstream `growth::kh1` definitions; their native menu entries are still
+copied verbatim. Disabled entries do not select a native lane. Combo/Air Combo Plus and Combo
+Master alone retain Valor. Outside an already imported aerial combo, a selected row outside
+the recognized ordinary C8..CE motion range is forwarded to KH1 regardless of the list,
+once. During imported air the native actor is parked in ground state 0, so its Attack
+placeholder may name a ground ability; that placeholder continues Valor air instead of
+starting a ground move at height. Real equipped air abilities prevent the imported air
+controller from entering. This avoids temporary native state writes for the selector.
+No native selector, ability flags,
+combo counter, ability inventory or finisher probability is fabricated. Native lanes use
+native primary contacts; their duplicate is cosmetic, without additional offhand contacts.
+The INI isolation option still affects imported Valor melee only, not these native routes.
+This is an explicit compatibility tradeoff, not per-swing mixing of both combo controllers.
+
+**Persistent cosmetic weapon (high as implementation; gameplay pending):** the duplicate's
+own queue draw may set its weapon mesh even when the primary draw has no weapon. It still
+requires the exact field actor/instance and a fresh pose for the current binding. Default
+actions follow a cached hand-local hold calibrated on a held locomotion pose, instead of a
+stowing/collapsing native primary weapon subtree. Every pose is rebuilt from the current
+native left hand and scoped to actor, instance, bone allocation, item and room generation.
+Unequip/rebind clears it. This changes no primary visibility flag or native action matrix.
+No duplicate damage/trail intent exists outside the imported attack controller.
+
+**New action matches:** read statically from the user's supplied Steam KH1 executable
+(link timestamp 1721645006), inspected privately; no executable bytes or disassembly are
+committed. Native request definitions below are not numeric physical MSET slot guesses.
+The regular file's second section contains u32 request descriptors (checked against the
+previously supplied native 118-record MSET). A live header must match the descriptor's
+motion metadata, with no pending native request. A mismatched bank/header remains native.
+
+| Native request | Valor donor | Evidence / confidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| 3E self item, 3F other target | ITEM 9 | KH1 command handler chooses by target identity; OpenKH KH2 motion dictionary names ITEM. High for roles, visual timing untested. |
+| 48 / 49 / 4A / 4B | Small front high/low, back high/low 10..13 | Steam flinch routine chooses direction by facing-dot and variant by hurt-part value 1. Direction high; high/low naming correspondence medium. |
+| 4C / 4D | Large front/back 23 / 24 | Native ground knockback facing variants. Semantic visual match, medium; KH1 keeps its own knockback. |
+| 4E / 4F and 50 / 51 | Air front/back 14 / 15 | Native air reaction facing variants, with different native push behavior. Semantic visual match, medium. |
+| Standing regular request 0, scripted actor | LINK_IDLE 6 if present | Native standing idle recognized at records 0/1. LINK_IDLE name from OpenKH. Its use as an interaction idle is derivative visual policy, not a verified universal talk gesture. |
+| Standing regular request 0, active event | Valor resolved field/no-weapon IDLE 0 | Loaded with KH2's own field-slot fallback from Valor's MSET, including that exact clip's root curve. Only regular standing idles, never an arbitrary EVM pose. |
+
+KH2 donor IDs and player-slot fallback are documented at
+https://openkh.dev/kh2/file/anb/mset.html ; native request roles also agree with the upstream
+item-use overlay (`pose::KH2_ITEM_USE`) and reaction code. No donor event, hitbox, voice,
+item script, damage/reaction controller, ability grant or invulnerability interval runs.
+KH1 keeps effects, item quantity/targets, damage, movement, events and cancels. Sampling uses
+native normalized time, including pauses; exact item-release gesture synchronization is not
+claimed. Missing donors leave KH1's current action intact.
+
+**Scene limits:** the field actor's existing default idle can be overlaid; dedicated scripted
+event-bank poses, other actors/copies, cinematics and unknown motions remain native. During
+recognized scene idles the native local motion of unretargeted children, including facial
+bones, is rebuilt under the retargeted parent, without feeding back our world matrices.
+No verified Valor counterpart was found here for chest opening, object lift/carry/throw,
+push or the five KH1 Trinities. Those keep native poses with a cosmetic duplicate where the
+regular Sora actor is drawn. There is no claim to replace every interaction or cutscene clip.
+
+**Validation:** synthetic tests cover equipped/disabled ability lanes, unknown-row pass-through,
+u32 request descriptor bounds, action/scene exclusions and clocks, fresh duplicate draw policy,
+binding-scoped native-hand attachment, collapsed calibration rejection and native child
+expression inheritance. Existing placement, trails, ability-table and contact tests remain.
+Windows/game execution, real Valor donor availability, item-release gesture sync and map/
+scene transitions still need a fresh-process game test. Results are recorded with the build.
+
