 # Combat model
 
+## Dual Wield prototype v6 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User policy:** Master Form's glide visual for KH1 Glide, Final Form's glide visual for
+Superglide, and Valor's combat idle for recognized cutscene standing idle. Slow the combat
+idle with an adjustable default of 75% of the donor's authored speed. KH1 retains native
+casting, action abilities, movement and ability gates; no Drive state or additional grants.
+
+| Native action | Donor | Clock |
+|---|---|---|
+| Glide, state 21, decoded player work +0x104 bit 0 clear | Master GLIDE 205 | Continuous native game time, authored rate |
+| Superglide, state 21, that bit set | Final GLIDE 205 | Continuous native game time, authored rate |
+| Ordinary idle and recognized regular cutscene standing idle | Valor battle-with-weapon IDLE 0 | Shared continuous clock, idle_speed = 0.75 by default |
+
+**Subtype source (high):** private inspection of the supplied Steam executable (timestamp
+1721645006) shows successful Glide start at Steam RVA 0x2B26C0 clearing bit 0 at decoded
+actor +0x148 player work +0x104. Superglide start at 0x2B2750 sets it after the same common
+start at 0x2B2D30. Both use state 21 and native request 0x71. Read that subtype rather than
+inferring it from equipped abilities, motion-slot guesses or velocity. An unreadable work
+pointer leaves the native pose intact. No new code hook or native work write is used.
+
+**Donors (high as implementation; appearance pending):** KH2's existing motion dictionary
+and player slot resolver supply GLIDE 205 from Master P_EX100_TRIF and Final P_EX100_ULTF.
+The optional donors require matching body clip metadata and two weapon rigs; missing data
+falls back to KH1. Only their visual data is loaded, with no script/effect archive. Passive
+form/controller selection stays Valor. Body, root removal and both weapons use the same
+source and sample frame. Final's right weapon placement is explicitly admitted by the
+visual source rather than Drive state; both blades retain its donor spacing. Native default
+actions still use the existing calibrated hand-local cosmetic duplicate. No glide contact,
+trail, scripted effect, sound, spell behavior, controller or growth ability is imported.
+
+**Clock source (high for units/limit; live pause behavior pending):** Epic RVA 0x23405DC /
+Steam 0x233FBDC is the upstream camera's native 60-Hz frame step (1 at 60fps, 2 at 30fps).
+The Steam time-update routine at 0x18D1F0 scales it, caps it at five and writes zero on its
+freeze branch. v6 accumulates validated finite 0..5 steps only in Panacea OnFrame. The
+physics callback also calls dual::frame, so that function must not advance this clock.
+Repeated render passes reuse the same time; zero steps hold. Local donor phase resets on
+action-family changes, explicit actor/weapon/room rebind, invalid data, backwards time or
+a sampling gap larger than five game frames. Combat-to-scene idle keeps the same phase.
+The donor is wrapped before its end frame, so a clamped native idle or nonlooping field
+clip cannot stop it. No wall-clock catch-up or native animation-speed write is used.
+Walk/run, jumps, items and damage keep their previous native-phase sampling.
+
+**Speed setting:** idle_speed in kh1-dual-wield.ini applies to ordinary combat and supported
+cutscene idle only; 1.0 means authored donor rate, 0.50 half speed. Finite 0.10..2.00 values
+are accepted; missing/invalid entries use 0.75. Restart reads configuration again. This is
+not 75% of v5's short-native-clip remapping, so the visible reduction can be larger.
+Interaction LINK_IDLE remains its separate donor. Dedicated event-bank gestures, other
+actors and cinematics retain native behavior, as in v5.
+
+**Validation:** synthetic tests cover subtype flags/unreadable data, donor isolation,
+config bounds, idle looping beyond native duration, repeated draws and pauses, shared
+combat/scene phase, 30/60/120fps-equivalent steps, invalid time and ownership/discontinuity
+resets. Existing native ability, contact, trail and attachment tests remain. Windows/game
+execution, actual donor availability, menu-pause timing, glide weapon placement and scene
+transitions require a fresh-process game test. No executable bytes or disassembly are shipped.
+
