 # Combat model
 
+## Dual Wield prototype v7 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User policy:** the cutscene idle must be the same slowed Valor combat idle; both native
+Glide and Superglide use Final Form's glide; the spinning displayed weapons can damage
+enemies. The passive ability still grants nothing else and native movement/casting remain.
+
+**Idle correction (high as code evidence; exact scene still unobserved):** v6 changed only
+the event/SceneIdle route to battle-with-weapon IDLE 0. A regular scripted standing idle
+without the global event flag still selected InteractionIdle / LINK_IDLE 6, with a different
+clock. v7 maps both to the same Valor combat IDLE 0, root, two-weapon pose, continuous clock
+family and idle_speed. Admission still requires normal standing state, regular idle record
+0/1, request 0 and a matching sampled header. It does not replace arbitrary EVM poses or
+gestures. Bounded SCENE IDLE ROUTE diagnostics record state, slot, request, event/script
+flags, regular-header agreement and chosen route for the user's next scene test. No claim
+is made that this explains every unprovided cutscene sample or that a dedicated event-bank
+idle has been identified. The slower gameplay idle path itself is unchanged.
+
+**Glide donor (user choice, high):** both actual native glide variants now select Final's
+GLIDE 205 and one continuous animation family. Master data is no longer loaded. The native
+player-work subtype bit remains diagnostic/selection evidence from v6, but does not switch
+donors, reset phase or open a new damage window. KH1 still requires its Glide/Superglide
+ability, and runs its speed, height, gravity, input, collision, landing and action changes.
+
+**Attack data (high from existing reader/research; runtime availability pending):**
+`docs/drive-model.md`, Final Form's floating Keyblades, documents weapon motion 205..207
+with ATKP 1281 right / 1282 left, group 2, power 100 and 30-frame re-hit intervals. That
+research used the user's KH2 data; the existing `kh2_rig::MotionHits` reader already admits
+these windows outside an action controller. v7 reads the live loaded GLIDE clip, filters
+only those two weapon/attack pairs and uses the loaded battle rows' power and interval,
+not a hard-coded damage amount. Body attacks, hover guards, jumps, spells and unrelated
+Final windows are excluded. The same keys persist across animation loops and glide subtype
+changes, so loops cannot grant an immediate extra hit. Each blade has its own key and the
+existing per-target records enforce the row interval. Physics uses validated native 60-Hz
+time-step units for those timers; repeated render passes never advance them or land damage.
+
+**Collision geometry (high as implementation; live alignment pending):** these remain
+duplicates of the equipped KH1 weapon, not KH2 weapon meshes. After the full body pose and
+both displayed grips succeed, the pose pass reads the existing native BONE_POINT routine's
+weapon start-to-tip samples and native basic-air weapon radius. It transforms the same
+range by the measured displayed right-to-left grip matrix for the duplicate. Thus contact
+extends along each visible blade and rotates with Final's blade bone, rather than using
+Sora's hand or a broad sphere around Sora. The straight native blade range is filled with
+overlapping spheres, including both ends, within the contact engine's 32 swept-shape cap;
+a radius/range combination too large to cover is rejected. Both arrays are published atomically with actor,
+instance, matrix allocation, weapon, room generation, frame, donor frame and actor position.
+The duplicate must have been successfully rebuilt by that exact pose call, not merely have
+a still-fresh pose from a previous action.
+
+**Scheduling/retirement (high as implementation):** native Sora physics consumes at most
+one complete sample per physics frame, after KH1's own movement. A sample from the current
+or immediately preceding physics frame can be translated by Sora's actual bounded movement
+since its draw. It is therefore limited by render/physics order (up to one frame of pose
+latency); no prediction of its next spin is claimed. A future/stale sample, changed binding,
+invalid shape or teleport is rejected. Missing draws clear swept geometry while retaining
+repeat-hit cooldowns for the same ongoing glide, so resuming the draw cannot create a
+damage burst or a long sweep from an old position. Landing, another action, loss of the
+passive ability, resource rebind, or loss of native eligibility retires the session.
+
+The existing `combat::Strikes` swept overlap, native enemy hurtparts, guard/wall/projectile
+checks, native attack constructor/contact/release and hit-record scaling are reused. A
+private Character value supplies aerial contact-row/reaction bookkeeping only; it is never
+stepped and never supplies displacement, input or a pose to Sora. Existing contact effects,
+sound, HP processing, reactions, drops and EXP stay native; no direct HP write is used.
+Guard/wall behavior follows that contact bridge, not a newly imported Final movement/recoil
+controller, so full KH2 action parity is not claimed. Magnet/holding follow-up movement is
+not run by the glide helper. No passive glide swing-trail request, script, voice, Drive
+gauge, invulnerability or ability grant is added. Offhand isolation can filter the right
+imported glide contact as it filters imported melee; native ability combos remain outside
+that option. Native combo-lane policy and default ground/air casting remain unchanged.
+
+**Validation:** synthetic coverage includes both scene flag routes sharing one donor/clock,
+glide subtype/loop continuity, tip versus palm and rotated duplicate geometry, invalid
+matrices/ranges, actor/weapon/room binding, frame freshness, movement translation and
+teleport rejection, per-blade window keys and repeat-hit spacing.
+Thin-blade coverage between native samples and a rotating tip crossing an enemy between
+frames are exercised, and repeat-hit timers are compared at 30/60/120fps-equivalent steps.
+The existing contact,
+trail, native ability and attachment regression suites remain. Native game execution,
+the specific cutscene, donor availability, effect/audio attribution, guards, glide collision
+alignment and hit intervals require a fresh-process test on the user's installation.
+
