 # Combat model
 
+## Dual Wield prototype v8 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User policy:** while Dual Wield is equipped, replace Guard with the attack Valor normally
+uses for the Guard/action button. It is an attack, not a defensive Guard. Preserve the
+other passive constraints and existing native attack-ability combo lanes.
+
+**Donor (high as existing code/data interpretation; installed data pending):** upstream
+`Character::try_action_button` already recognizes a moveset's row 11 with no Guard window
+as an attack. Its Valor notes identify a rising double slash with a 90-unit hop; the
+existing `guard_row_attack_launches_from_square` simulation covers standing and walking.
+v7's base filter removed all non-air ground-hop rows, including that row. v8 retains only
+this explicit kind-0, ability-0 ground row when its loaded clip contains a weapon hit window
+and no Guard window. The body donor must also exist in the loaded rig. The exact motion,
+hop, hit/trail windows and ATKP power remain from the user's data, not a guessed animation
+number. Ordinary rows cannot sub-select it: their old references are severed while it is
+absent, then the explicit row is appended with no sub. It is reached by the action button.
+Other ability-dependent moves and automatic ground hops remain filtered. No Guard or other
+ability is injected into the imported character or saved ability list.
+
+**Native selection evidence (high):** private inspection of the supplied Steam executable
+(timestamp 1721645006) confirms ability init at Steam 0x2A670A..0x2A672D sets flags 0x10
+for equipped native Guard (21) and 0x20 for Dodge Roll (22), in Steam 0x2D5EC10 / Epic
+0x2D5F610. Native action dispatch at Steam 0x2A7BCB..0x2A7C9E requires a Square action
+bit 0x04000000 and ground state 0, rejects deep water, then picks Guard when 0x10 is set
+and either Roll is absent or stats +8 exceeds the move-vector +0xC magnitude. Other cases
+retain native Roll/no-action. A chosen menu command or jump has priority. The existing
+control hook runs the same conservative selector before forwarding native control, with
+can-act, event/script, shortcut/submenu and finite/readability guards. The existing mapped
+deep-water function (Epic 0x2BF530 / Steam 0x2C16E0) is reused. No executable bytes or
+disassembly are shipped, and no new function hook/address table entry is added.
+
+**Ownership (high as implementation; native timing pending):** only a selected native
+Guard with a ready duplicate/donor queues one imported action press. Its native Square
+action bit is consumed before the original control callback runs, preventing the native
+defensive object; native movement and other input still run. The hook
+uses the existing temporary Square-bit masking/restoration pattern on the merged native
+button state too, including keyboard input; the logical L1 state protects shortcuts.
+The one-session Guard exception allows the imported rising attack even when an ordinary combo lane is native due to
+equipped action abilities. Known native action slots may hand over after the proven Guard
+selection, rather than blocking it as an unrelated stale native action. Existing actor,
+scene, control, pose, timeout and interruption guards continue to apply. The queued press
+has priority on its first controller step and clears on cancellation/rebind/unequip.
+Raw Square during an unrelated imported combo cannot start the ability-free donor row:
+the action input is admitted only for a session established by native Guard selection.
+
+The existing controller runs this attack and its hop; DUAL_AIR_ACTIVE tracks its airborne
+state, so completion/interruption resumes native fall at the current height. A following
+native ability Attack waits for a valid command/cancel window, restores that native air
+state before the original selector runs, and keeps its native row/timing. Other accepted
+ordinary imported Attack requests retire the Guard exception. Existing contact, per-hand
+trail and offhand-isolation paths apply to the new attack. No defensive Guard or native
+Guard ability is granted. Native Guard needs to be equipped to select this replacement;
+unequipping Dual Wield restores the original Guard behavior. Moving Square still chooses
+Dodge Roll under KH1's own rule when it is equipped; air Glide and spell shortcuts stay native.
+
+**Validation:** tests exercise native Guard/Roll threshold and ability gates, jump/menu/air
+exclusions, valid versus missing/defensive donor data, filtering/fallback references,
+ordinary Attack exclusion and a real Character simulation of the rising attack with both
+weapon hits, trails, no guard boxes, upward movement and completion into free air. Existing
+native ability, idle, glide, contact and retirement suites remain. Fresh-process gameplay
+is required to confirm the input edge, actual Valor row, launch, contact/trails, native
+ability follow-ups and restoration on unequip. No game execution is claimed here.
