 # Combat model
 
+## Dual styles prototype v9 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User policy:** rename Dual Wield to **Style: Dual Close** and add **Style: Dual Ranged**.
+Ranged replaces the same admitted non-melee action visuals with Final Form, adds Final
+casting visuals over KH1's existing spells, disables Attack and every route into melee,
+and retains physical contacts from the floating weapons during other animations. Equipping
+either style must unequip the other. No Drive gauge, transformation or extra native ability.
+
+### Saved abilities and switching (derived policy; portable tests)
+
+Close retains id126 and its existing equipped/disabled byte. Ranged uses the unused id125,
+initially disabled, zero AP. Avoid id127's disabled 0xFF byte. The native 65 ability records
+are copied exactly; only the two custom records and unused table padding are changed.
+Append only into a verified empty save-list tail, without evicting a native entry. A native
+menu equip toggles one byte; if both style bytes are on, disable the previously selected
+style in place. A separate saved-choice tracker survives runtime/model suspension. A
+pre-existing ambiguous both-on save selects Ranged once. Only our two IDs are ever disabled
+by exclusivity or removed by remove_dual_wield. Other ability states, AP and order remain.
+
+Changing style uses the existing native aerial handoff, then retires the imported
+controller, queued Guard/Attack press, native-cast observer, geometry, emitters and draw
+bindings. A new generation prevents either style from consuming the other's old poses.
+Close retains v8's Valor combos, equipped native attack-ability lane priority, Guard attack,
+Final glides, cosmetics and native casting. Ranged can never request the Valor controller
+or its Guard attack. Its native defensive Guard and Dodge Roll stay native when equipped.
+
+### Native attack restrictions (existing hooks + privately checked Steam anchors)
+
+Ranged marks Attack and physical-special command IDs disabled after KH1's menu fill. It
+also refuses them at menu selection and before native command dispatch, including all
+Sonic Blade, Ars Arcanum, Strike Raid, Ragnarok and Trinity Limit follow-ups. The native
+physical-special offer call is suppressed while Ranged is active. Talk/Open/Examine and
+native spell, item, summon and partner commands remain native. The menu hook has no
+full-overhaul spell-to-attack buffering behavior: Close/Off forward it directly.
+
+The already-hooked native execute-attack-row function is a final Ranged gate for native
+ability/counterattack rows, independent of the command word. Floating contacts use the
+separate existing constructor/contact bridge, so they do not enter this forbidden attack
+selection path. No Final combo rows, magic scripts, Drive state or body-spell hitboxes run.
+
+Existing Epic RVAs 0x292330 (menu fill), 0x2912F0 (selection), 0x292B12 (special offer call)
+and 0x28AF60 (offer routine) already have Steam mappings. Their expected prologues and
+exact call target match the supplied Steam executable (link timestamp 1721645006). These
+are static checks, not proof of live hook execution. Startup requires all new hooks to
+match before it grants/enables either style. No executable/disassembly bytes are shipped.
+
+### Final visuals and casting (runtime donor data; existing motion dictionary)
+
+Every previous admitted movement, damage, item and recognized interaction/scene-idle
+visual selects Final instead of Valor in Ranged. Both native glides still select Final 205.
+Combat and recognized scene standing idle share Final IDLE 0 and the existing idle_speed
+clock. Unmatched native actions and missing donors retain native body poses/cosmetic
+hand-following duplicate. Both floating weapon poses are sampled with the body, including
+the actual blade-bone spin, with donor root travel removed. KH1 owns movement and physics.
+
+Final casts use the existing documented native-to-donor mapping, for all native levels:
+
+| KH1 spell | Final ground / air motion |
+|---|---|
+| Fire | 56 / 58 |
+| Blizzard | 59 / 61 |
+| Thunder, Gravity | 62 / 64 |
+| Cure, Stop, Aero | 65 / 67 |
+
+The four matching spell families follow Final's MAGC motion convention documented below.
+Gravity/Stop/Aero are an explicit visual fallback policy, not KH2 versions of those spells.
+Observe a real changed native request or restarted cast after native command execution,
+then wait for the exact regular-bank header/request to agree. Queued repeated casts may
+not latch the previous clip. The donor follows normalized native clip time, never loops,
+and is retired on interruption, pointer/clock/binding change, timeout or style switch.
+KH1 retains MP, cast rate/recovery, targeting, projectiles, effects, sound and damage. No
+Final elemental damage multipliers or KH2 spell scripts are applied. Exact visible release
+sync and all ground/air native state transitions still need a game recording.
+
+### Floating contacts without attacks (extends v7's physics-only contact bridge)
+
+For Ranged, capture the displayed equipped-weapon start-to-tip geometry at both actual
+floating grips during admitted non-melee Final poses. Scene idles are visual only. At the
+next native physics step require matching style generation, exact action, current binding,
+finite/bounded positions and a current/previous-frame pose. Only the shown clip's actual
+weapon1/weapon2 Hitbox windows pass through MotionHits; Guard and body/spell windows do not.
+Close remains restricted to its existing Final glide windows (1281/1282).
+
+Reuse native hurtparts, eligibility, walls, projectile clashes, constructor/contact/release,
+power, re-hit intervals and impact sound/effects. No direct HP writes or swept geometry
+across missing draws/action transitions. Preserve cooldowns during a missing pose and
+reset the sweep on a new motion. Refresh ground/air contact-row bookkeeping when KH1's
+actual movement state changes, without stepping a donor controller. The bookkeeping
+Character has an empty moveset: even an accidental future step cannot select an attack or
+cast. No automatic combo follow-up or continuous swing-trail emitter is added. The existing
+offhand_only_test option can still isolate the left imported contacts in either style.
+
+**Validation:** 307 local tests passed across 18 suites, including 78 Dual Wield tests.
+The Windows x64 release cross-build passed with one codegen unit for kh1-hook; the default
+parallel codegen emitted empty object files in this environment. PE exports/imports and
+three added native hook anchors were checked. The attached Valor MSET was inspected (37
+nonempty motion entries); Final assets still load from the user's KH2 installation and
+are not available here. Actual game execution, ability-menu refresh/exclusivity, Final
+appearance/casting sync, passive contacts and map transitions remain unverified here.
+
 ## Dual Wield prototype v8 derivative (2026-10-30)
 
 **User policy:** while Dual Wield is equipped, replace Guard with the attack Valor normally
