+## Dual styles prototype v10 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User report:** casting Fire crashed v9. No crash log was supplied. Source inspection
+found a concrete invalid-read path in every observed Ranged cast: dual_cast::observed
+called reflect::kh1_spell_level for a diagnostic level value. That helper reads its
+private BASE + SPELLS_RVA (0x2D23580, translated for Steam), then a save pointer fallback.
+Reflect's BASE is initialized only by reflect::install. The isolated OnInit deliberately
+never installs Reflect, so this path reads an unmapped low address instead of game memory.
+This defect matches the reported trigger; the exact user exception remains unconfirmed.
+
+**Fix:** remove the optional-module lookup and unused NativeCast level field entirely.
+The native spell id and grounded/aerial mode already select the Final visual family for
+all native levels. The observer now uses only its guarded actor/request snapshots,
+current binding/frame and the pure NativeCast clock. It needs no spell-level table,
+save-level fallback or Reflect initialization. Accepted-cast diagnostics omit the unused
+level rather than report a guessed one. KH1 continues to select the actual spell level,
+MP cost, effects, projectile, damage and recovery without any new writes or hooks.
+
+All v9 behavior remains: exclusive Close/Ranged abilities, Final non-melee/casting visuals,
+Ranged attack/physical-special restrictions, current equipped-weapon duplication and
+physics-only floating weapon contacts. No casting animation was disabled as a workaround.
+No other overhaul module is initialized or granted.
+
+**Validation:** 308 local tests passed in 18 suites, including 79 Dual Wield tests. A new
+regression exercises the cast clock and visual family for all seven spells in ground/air
+without any level-table input. Existing queued/repeated-cast, invalid-pointer/time,
+interruption and rebind tests remain. Windows x64 release cross-build (one codegen unit)
+and PE exports/imports passed. Ranged observer dependency inspection finds no remaining
+Reflect/optional-module level call. The menu/offer hook anchors are unchanged from v9 and
+reuse its static executable checks. No Windows/game execution or observed crash-log
+confirmation is claimed; a fresh-process ground/air Fire test is still required.
+
