 # Combat model
 
+## Dual styles prototype v11 derivative (2026-10-30)
+
+**User policy (high):** Close Glide and Superglide hold both weapons and cause no spinning
+blade damage. Ranged regular Glide keeps going while held, stops descending near the floor,
+and ends on release. Ranged's basic ground/air combo repeats its existing Aero body/two-blade
+pose for every attack slot; no Aero spell effects. Existing finite combo endings still apply.
+
+### Held Close glides
+
+The native Glide/Superglide action now deliberately falls through to KH1's own body/primary
+weapon pose. The existing actor-bound, palm-calibrated cosmetic duplicate follows its left
+hand, including when no held-pose calibration has been seen yet (the v9 idle calibration
+fallback). No Final glide overlay or passive contact session is admitted in Close; the
+passive hit filter now accepts only Ranged. Native movement and ability gates stay native.
+This uses known KH1 held animations rather than inventing a Valor glide donor it lacks.
+
+### Ranged regular Glide floor clamp
+
+**Native source:** private inspection of the supplied Steam executable (stamp 1721645006).
+Glide's registered displacement callback is Steam RVA 0x2B2A20 (Epic 0x2B0890) and native
+held-input callback is Steam 0x2B2BF0 (Epic 0x2B0A60). The per-player work +0x104 bit 0
+separates Superglide; regular Glide's input reads held bit 4 at input +4. Work +0x100
+is its initial input/release grace timer. Descent comes from actor +0x3C4, ground distance
+from actor +0x3D4. Whole position-independent hook instructions, subtype/height/input operands
+and registration targets are privately checked against Steam; runtime operand/prologue
+checks fail closed. Epic offsets follow this section's established mapping and must pass
+the same runtime checks; this turn has no Epic executable execution/verification.
+
+**Adaptation:** after the original displacement callback, clamp only positive downward
+movement to max(height - 1, 0), and keep its stored descent equal to that output. One native
+unit is a deliberate small collision clearance, not a claim that vanilla has a one-unit
+termination threshold. This makes ordinary level-floor Glide hover just above collision.
+No stored world altitude or stale floor is reused. On real button release, clear only the
+active regular Glide's input grace timer before forwarding the original callback once.
+All other modes/actors, Superglide, scenes, held/scripted/damaged Sora and controller-owned
+attacks forward unchanged. No ground start, ability grant, forced state or teleport is added.
+KH1 still resolves walls, terrain, moving platforms, water and interruptions; steep terrain
+can legitimately collide/end the action. Exact near-ground behavior needs a game test.
+
+### Ranged Aero-pose basic combo
+
+The existing Aero visual maps to Final's Cure-family body/weapon motion 65 on the ground,
+67 in air; both are already used by the native Aero cast observer. A separate Character is
+built from those clips. Four explicit rows select that same pose for ordinary/finisher slots
+on ground/air, with self-substitution for intentional same-motion repeats and no hop/lunge.
+The existing controller uses a three-slot base, equipped Combo Plus/Air Combo Plus, Combo
+Master, actual contacts and the prior one-swing-on-miss rule. A press during the authored
+last-quarter combo window can advance; no automatic loop or spell-to-attack followup runs.
+The last finisher must finish; air combos keep their usual landing boundary.
+
+The adapted clips have zero movement roots and no events. Only real weapon 1/2 Hitbox
+windows survive, plus explicit last-quarter Combo/ComboMagic/Finisher windows. Body hits,
+Guard/invulnerability/no-gravity/script/spell events are removed. The original Final
+Character is never stepped: its root curve is read by RigAnim to remove authored motion
+from the displayed skeleton. Native spells continue through the v10 observer and retain
+actual KH1 MP/levels/effects/projectiles/damage. No spell command, Aero cast or spell FX is
+created by Attack. Physical limit commands/followups remain blocked; native melee row
+execution is intercepted, including equipped attack abilities. Close's ability priority
+and rising Guard action are retained; Ranged Guard remains native if already equipped.
+
+Owned Ranged attacks now retarget/float both weapons with Final's source, and publish the
+same completed body/two-weapon blade geometry as passive poses. The attack controller's
+own swing ids, per-hand hit records, re-hit intervals and actual hit qualification feed
+native contacts, with no native melee object underneath. Same actor/weapon/room generation,
+at most one physics-frame-old geometry, finite/teleport bounds and <=5 donor-frame phase
+lag are required. A repeated pose at frame zero rejects its previous swing's endpoint.
+Missing draws clear sweeps and do not grant hits. Passive pose logic does not run while
+an attack owns Sora. Offhand-only test filtering still applies to these contacts.
+
+### Validation and limits
+
+Portable regressions cover finite repeated ground/air combos and combo modifiers, finisher
+endings, whiffs/held input, donor event/root/body-window stripping, missing clips, same-motion
+geometry restarts, Close glide exclusion and bounded regular-Glide descent. New hook receipts
+contain addresses and booleans only, no executable bytes. Existing casting, binding, geometry,
+ability priority and retirement checks remain. All 316 tests passed in 18 suites, including 87 Dual Wield tests. Windows cross-build/PE,
+archive CRC and full-extraction verification are recorded with the completed v11 package.
+No Windows/game execution or installed Final donor validation is claimed here.
+
